------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Presentations of groups
--
-- One-qubit completeness
--
-- On one wire the generators are ω, X and T and the relations are R₁,
-- R₇, R₁₀ and R₁₁: the presented group is ℤ₈ × D₁₆, the scalars times
-- the dihedral group of order 16 generated by T and X (the paper's
-- footnote 1).  Every one-wire circuit is equal to ω^k T^a X^e with
-- k, a ∈ ℤ₈ and e ∈ ℤ₂ — the paper's normal form at width one, a
-- scalar, a T-block and an X-block — and distinct such circuits
-- denote distinct operators.
--
-- The normal form is computed by an automaton reading the circuit
-- letter by letter (`run`); that it is a normal form for the
-- congruence is that the automaton respects the relations (run-cong,
-- decided) and that its states read back as the circuits reaching
-- them (run-sound).  Uniqueness is decided on the 128 stored
-- operators.  Completeness is then the library's by-normalization,
-- packaged by StarPresentation.MonoidSem as a sub-monoid presentation
-- of the operators.
------------------------------------------------------------------------

{-# OPTIONS --cubical-compatible --safe #-}

module Examples.Groups.CNOT-Dihedral.OneQubit where

